# ANV-0056 -- the audit resolved a live intent against the wrong range's record
#
# A record lives on the range that owns its transaction's *primary* key and
# nowhere else (record.h). audited_value looked for it on the range the
# *intent* sat on, which finds nothing for every cross-range transaction -- the
# transactions this phase exists to exercise -- so the audit read past the
# intent to the version from before the transaction.
seed        = 1 and 7 (bank, snapshot isolation)
workload    = txn_bank, kBank
nodes       = 5
keys        = 16 x 100 = 1600, neighbourhood 4
faults      = drawn from seed; needs only a cross-range transfer whose secondary
              intent has not been lazily resolved by the time the audit runs,
              which is the common case after settle because settle has no
              clients left to read anything
invariant   = the bank's conserved total (workload)
reproduce   = anvil_txn_faults 30
expect      = before the fix, seed 1 reports `the cluster holds 1583 and started
              with 1600` and seed 7 reports 1585/1600, both with converged=yes.
              Both shortfalls are smaller than one account because each is one
              half of one transfer: the debit's range had materialised its
              version and the credit's range still held an unresolved intent.
              After the fix, 30/30 seeds at all three levels.
note        = api_visible: no. The money was never missing; the audit could not
              see it. The rejected alternative -- searching every range for the
              record -- is recorded in CONTEXT.md section 14 and must not be
              re-tried: it accepts any replica anywhere that says kCommitted,
              which reconstructs the total the engine should have had.
